  { q: "Who are Niulang and Zhinü?", a: "They are the Cowherd and Weaver Girl in a Chinese myth. In a common version, the Milky Way separates them and magpies form a bridge so they can meet once a year on Qixi." },
  { q: "What did people traditionally do for Qixi?", a: "Practices varied by place. Institutional records describe offerings of fruit, needle-threading contests, worship connected with the Cowherd and Weaver Girl, and other ways of asking for skill." },
];

